From b0899a3dafa578c04ee064878bb66e6ed9f71362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 01:46:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix: CRLF line endings + nginx startup crash

Two critical fixes:

1. CRLF Line Ending Bug (entrypoint.sh 'no such file or directory')
   - Root cause: Git on Windows converts LF -> CRLF on checkout.
     When Docker copies the file, the shebang becomes #!/bin/bash\r
     which Linux cannot execute.
   - Fix: Added .gitattributes that enforces LF for ALL text files,
     especially shell scripts (*.sh, entrypoint.sh).
   - After pulling this commit, users must renormalize their working
     copy: git rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard

2. Nginx Startup Crash (host not found in upstream 'rcerp_app')
   - Root cause: nginx resolves the PHP-FPM upstream hostname at
     startup. If the app container isn't running yet, nginx crashes
     with 'emerg: host not found in upstream'.
   - Fix: Changed fastcgi_pass from 'rcerp_app:9000' to use a
     variable ($app_upstream) + Docker DNS resolver (127.0.0.11).
     This defers DNS resolution to request time, so nginx starts
     even when the app container isn't ready yet.

3. Added .gitattributes to .dockerignore (not needed in build context)
---
 .dockerignore             |  1 +
 .gitattributes            | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 docker/nginx/default.conf | 26 +++++++++++++++++------
 3 files changed, 64 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 .gitattributes

